\title{webrarian: Bundle and Deploy 'webR' Instances}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.svg}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

The 'webR' (\url{https://docs.r-wasm.org/webr/}) project runs R in a web browser through 'WebAssembly'. This package turns a folder of R scripts, data files and package names into a static web site that opens an in-browser workspace (editor, console, files, plots and environment) with those packages and files already in place, and previews it locally. Sites deploy to 'GitHub Pages', 'Netlify' or any static host and can be built to run fully offline; collection_mirror() builds a self-contained 'webR' site and package repository for networks without internet access. Local and 'GitHub' packages are compiled to 'WebAssembly' with 'Docker'.
}
\section{Package options}{

Build downloads are cached, so a rebuild reuses them. These settings
control the cache, the webR version and the CRAN comparison:
\itemize{
\item \strong{Where the cache is.} \code{tools::R_user_dir("webrarian", "cache")}. Set
the \code{R_USER_CACHE_DIR} environment variable to move it (webrarian's cache
is then its \code{R/webrarian} subdirectory). \code{\link[=webr_cache_info]{webr_cache_info()}} shows what is
there and \code{\link[=webr_cache_clear]{webr_cache_clear()}} removes it. After each webR engine
download, only the three most recently used engines are kept, and cached
packages are removed for R versions that neither those engines nor this
webrarian's own engines use.
\item \strong{\code{webrarian.package_cache} option, \code{WEBRARIAN_PACKAGE_CACHE} environment
variable.} This is a switch, not a path. Set either to \code{FALSE} (or
\code{"0"}) to make every build download its packages afresh. The option wins when both are
set. A cached package is reused only when its checksum matches the
repository's.
\item \strong{\code{WEBRARIAN_WEBR_VERSION} environment variable.} The webR version used
when \verb{_webrarian.yml} names none, for new collections, and for
\code{\link[=collection_mirror]{collection_mirror()}}. It must be a version tested with this webrarian,
or a patch release on the same line (accepted with a warning).
\item \strong{\code{webrarian.cran_repo} option.} The repository \code{\link[=check_inventory]{check_inventory()}} and
\code{\link[=bind]{bind()}} compare WebAssembly package versions with, given as a URL, or
\code{FALSE} to skip the comparison. Unset, it is the CRAN mirror in \code{getOption("repos")},
else \verb{https://cloud.r-project.org}. Its index is read at most once a day
and kept in the user cache, and so is a failed read. When it cannot be
reached the CRAN versions are \code{NA}, and nothing is printed or fails.
}
